{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T21:27:47.547Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8a4268fe12c2a5f9fcd4da8d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1642","claim:pm-gh1643","claim:pm-gh1644","lineage:pm-gh1642","lineage:pm-5t33or","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1642+pm-gh1643+pm-gh1644","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1642","claim:pm-gh1643","claim:pm-gh1644","lineage:pm-gh1642","lineage:pm-5t33or","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-hke9z7"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"MCP read tools silently ignore declared flat parameters: pm_context reads none, and for/tokenBudget/depth on pm_list, pm_search, pm_next and pm_get never reach the intent layer"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Discovered while verifying pm-gh1644 over MCP (published 2026.10.31 and current source both reproduce).\n\nEvery narrow MCP read tool declares its action parameters flat in its inputSchema (pm_context declares for, limit, depth, section, fields, tokenBudget, ...; pm_list/pm_search/pm_next/pm_get declare for and tokenBudget). The SDK runtime only moves a flat argument into the options record the handlers read when it appears in the hand-maintained HOISTED_ACTION_OPTION_KEYS table in src/sdk/runtime-input.ts. That table has no context entry at all and omits for/tokenBudget (and most filters) from list, search, next and get. A flat argument outside the table is accepted without a warning (it is declared) and then dropped.\n\nMeasured in a fresh sandbox through the MCP tools/call handler, flat vs nested options: pm_context {depth: deep} → depth brief (nested → deep); pm_context {for: orient, limit: 10} → no intent, limit null, token_budget 1600 (nested → orient, limit 3); pm_list {for: triage}, pm_search {query, for: discover}, pm_next {for: execute}, pm_get {id, for: inspect} → no context_intent receipt (nested → applied); pm_next {limit: 1} → 5 rows (nested → 1). The declared intent layer is therefore unreachable for MCP hosts that send the flat arguments the schema advertises. Same defect family as pm-wcaa (pm_files declared-but-ignored params, closed individually) and pm-hno5.\n\nDuplicate search: 'MCP pm_context flat arguments ignored options', 'MCP declared parameter silently ignored', 'mcp for intent not applied' — no open item."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","context","contracts","mcp"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-31T21:27:47.547Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T21:27:47.547Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"For context, get, list, next and search, every optional parameter the action's tool contract declares is hoisted from flat MCP arguments into the handler options (derived from PM_TOOL_ACTION_PARAMETER_CONTRACTS, not a hand list), nested options still win; flat and nested calls produce identical results for for, limit, depth and tokenBudget on all five tools; a regression test iterates every declared optional key of the five actions and fails if one is not hoisted"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5k4v"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"An MCP host that sends the flat parameters a read tool's schema declares gets the same intent, projection and limits as the nested options form."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1644","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-10-31T21:27:47.547Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-hno5","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-31T21:27:47.547Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-wcaa","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-31T21:27:47.547Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"6dbc88b03472e9eb3f3f58b362c375231c56b2afa66c996a0a90add54340e992","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a0334c493436144b67d1076e4d4c5be646759351c684aad3cbdb3c6b71305080"}
